vkquake-ios overlay 0016: warn when the rerelease localization table
resolved to a placeholder.

Upstream 050b9f19 now reads localization/loc_<lang>.txt through
COM_LoadFile (the pak-aware VFS) before the loose-file and kpf paths, so
the pak-vs-kpf ordering this overlay used to carry is gone -- it IS
upstream now. What upstream still does not do is say anything when the
one broken data combination shows up.

That combination is pre-2026 game paks (no localization/ entry) sitting
next to a 2026-or-later QuakeEX.kpf, whose loc_*.txt are 27-byte
`placeholder = "placeholder"` stubs. LOC_LoadFile "succeeds" with a
single entry, LOC_GetString then returns every key verbatim, and the
player sees $qc_item_health on screen with nothing in the log to explain
it. Both clean vintages already work; this is purely a report.

--- a/Quake/common.c
+++ b/Quake/common.c
@@ -4148,6 +4148,21 @@
 	}
 
 	Con_Printf ("Loaded %d strings from '%s'\n", localization.numentries, file);
+
+	// vkquake-ios: diagnose the one game-data combination that otherwise fails
+	// SILENTLY -- pre-2026 paks (no localization/ entry) next to a 2026-or-later
+	// QuakeEX.kpf, whose loc_*.txt are 27-byte `placeholder = "placeholder"` stubs.
+	// LOC_LoadFile "succeeds" with a single entry, LOC_GetString then returns every
+	// key verbatim, and the player sees $qc_item_health on screen with nothing in
+	// the log to explain it. The two CLEAN vintages are already handled by the
+	// search order upstream, so this is purely a report: in this mixed case there
+	// are no strings anywhere to recover.
+	if (localization.numentries <= 2)
+		Con_Warning (
+			"localized text is UNAVAILABLE: '%s' resolved to a placeholder.\n"
+			"Your game paks predate the 2026 update but QuakeEX.kpf is from it or later.\n"
+			"Re-copy the WHOLE rerelease folder (id1/pak0.pak carries the strings now).\n",
+			file);
 }
 
